questions.prompt:
This Express handler is used to claim a unique username. Two people sometimes end up with the same name. Find the bug and fix it.

```js
app.post('/claim', async (req, res) => {
  const { name } = req.body;
  const existing = await db.query('SELECT 1 FROM users WHERE name = $1', [name]);
  if (existing.rows.length > 0) return res.status(409).send('taken');
  await db.query('INSERT INTO users(name) VALUES ($1)', [name]);
  res.send('ok');
});
```

questions.answer:
```sql
ALTER TABLE users ADD CONSTRAINT users_name_key UNIQUE (name);
```
```js
const r = await db.query(
  'INSERT INTO users(name) VALUES ($1) ON CONFLICT (name) DO NOTHING', [name]);
if (r.rowCount === 0) return res.status(409).send('taken');
res.send('ok');
```

questions.prompt:
Write a small `Semaphore` class for Node (no libraries) so you can limit concurrency, e.g. at most 3 simultaneous calls to a slow API:

```js
const sem = new Semaphore(3);
await Promise.all(urls.map(async (u) => {
  const release = await sem.acquire();
  try { return await fetch(u); } finally { release(); }
}));
```

questions.answer:
```js
class Semaphore {
  constructor(n) { this.free = n; this.waiters = []; }
  acquire() {
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
      const grant = () => {
        let done = false;
        resolve(() => {
          if (done) return; done = true;
          const next = this.waiters.shift();
          if (next) next(); else this.free++;
        });
      };
      if (this.free > 0) { this.free--; grant(); }
      else this.waiters.push(grant);
    });
  }
}
```
